      "name": "guarded_magnitude",
      "source_file": "guarded_magnitude.verbose",
      "source": "@verbose 0.1.0\n\nconcept Movement\n  @intention: \"Bound signed quantity and integer unit price before calculating magnitude\"\n  @source: guarded_magnitude.intent:1\n  fields:\n    quantity : number [-1000, 1000]\n    unit_price : number [0, 1000000]\n\nrule magnitude\n  @intention: \"Calculate absolute movement value with explicit nonzero and positive magnitude guards\"\n  @source: guarded_magnitude.intent:2\n  input:\n    item : Movement\n  output:\n    out : number\n  logic:\n    out = if item.quantity != 0 then if abs(item.quantity) > 0 then abs(item.quantity) * item.unit_price else 0 else 0\n  proofs:\n    purity:\n      reads : [item.quantity, item.unit_price]\n      calls : []\n    termination:\n      bound : 30\n  hints:\n    overflow : [0, 1000000000]\n",
      "intent_file": "guarded_magnitude.intent",
      "intent": "Quantity is an integer in [-1000, 1000] and unit price is an integer in [0, 1000000].\nFor nonzero quantity, multiply its positive absolute magnitude by unit price; otherwise return zero. Verify all branches before removing the redundant magnitude test.\n",
